  {
   "_comment": "v0.16.1 finding 23 -- THE COMBAT-BEAT CLOCK. Every row keyed on attack_resolved / combatant_downed / skill_resolved / reaction_triggered now listens to `ui_combat_beat` and matches the original event id through `beat_type`. Reason: WICombatAI.take_turn emits an entire AI turn SYNCHRONOUSLY, so footsteps, attack, downed and the sting all reached the raw bus at t=0 while combat_playback.drain() unspooled the visuals one beat_delay() apart -- a kill after a 3-cell approach was heard ~1.5-2s before it was seen, worst of all for the player's own death (which by definition happens on an enemy turn). combat_screen emits UI_COMBAT_BEAT from BOTH paths: the live player turn in the same frame as the sim (timing unchanged), the playback path at DEQUEUE, beside the animation. `dashed` and `combat_finished` are DELIBERATELY still raw -- scope stays this set.",
